<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Cairn raised at Lehman.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Cairn raised at Lehman.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cairn Energy Plc was raised to &quot;outperform&quot; from &quot;neutral&quot; at Lehman Brothers, the investment bank said on Monday.</p>
<p>Analysts at Lehman said the stock had dropped 24 percent from their mid-March high, even as the newsflow from the company had improved, primarily because of its alliance with Shell to develop oil fields in Bangladesh.</p>
<p>The stock was unchanged at 481-1/2p by 0825 GMT.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
